From 59031690f5a5328a06021d3c95e5cc79f14e9c19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:04:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 069/110] media: i2c: add Samsung S5K4ECGX sensor driver

The S5K4ECGX is a 5 MP sensor with its own ISP and a two-lane MIPI
CSI-2 output delivering UYVY; it is the rear camera of the Samsung
Galaxy Tab E 9.6 (SM-T560). Mainline had a driver for it until v6.0
(removed with the unused board files); it loaded its setup from a
firmware blob too, but in a different format.

The register settings exist only in the stock Android camera HAL, so
the driver loads them as firmware: s5k4ecgx/init.bin and one table per
preview size, little-endian {u16 reg, u16 val} pairs with 0xffff NNNN
meaning a delay of NNNN ms. Most entries go through the indirect
interface into the ISP's RAM (0x0028/0x002a address, 0x0f12 data with
auto increment), which the driver tracks while writing.

The HAL's init table ends by enabling the preview. The driver skips
those two words, writes the size table and then enables the preview
with REG_G_ENABLE_PREV/REG_G_ENABLE_PREV_CHG, as the former mainline
driver did; disabling uses the same pair. pre_streamon only powers the
sensor up, so the lanes idle in LP-11 while the receiver brings up its
D-PHY. Init and size table are written again when the size changes
(the size tables also touch other ISP settings). The link runs at
344 Mbit/s per lane for all sizes.

Only the preview path is supported: 640x480, 800x480, 960x960,
1024x768, 1280x720, 1280x768. The capture sizes of the HAL, up to
2576x1932, need its capture sequence.

Power sequence as the vendor kernel: I/O and analog supply, MCLK
(24 MHz), the external 1.2 V core supply, powerdown and reset released.
Probe checks the firmware version word (0x4ec0).

Tested on the Galaxy Tab E 9.6 with the SC7730 DCAM driver: all six
sizes stream without errors (11 fps in a dim room), switching between
sizes and between rear and front camera works, white balance settles
within a few seconds after the init.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig    |  16 +
 drivers/media/i2c/Makefile   |   1 +
 drivers/media/i2c/s5k4ecgx.c | 600 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 617 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/i2c/s5k4ecgx.c

